    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who commands our top efficiency score at 80.98. His prime spot at the top of the order against Michael McGreevy, combined with an elite sprint speed profile, makes him our premier asset for the stolen base category. **Yordan Alvarez** (66.84) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.79) follow closely as our most reliable power threats; **Yordan Alvarez** maintains an elite 0.464 xwOBA despite facing a neutral matchup, while **Kyle Schwarber** benefits significantly from leading off against Connor Prielipp. Additionally, **Lars Nootbaar** (64.61) and **Junior Caminero** (64.47) are strong starts, with **Lars Nootbaar** benefiting from a highly favorable +11% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage against Grant Holmes.\n\nStrategic lineup construction today heavily weights platoon utility. **Dillon Dingler** (63.90) and **Trea Turner** (63.78) are locked in as efficient contributors, with **Trea Turner** specifically highlighted for his ability to pressure the basepaths even against an elite hold pitcher. Our most difficult decision centered on the utility slot, where **Nelson Velazquez** (43.81) narrowly missed the cut. While **Nelson Velazquez** showed potential against Emerson Hancock, the optimizer ultimately favored the higher-upside efficiency of our starters, particularly those with cleaner pathways to run production. Owners should remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Gary Sanchez**, as his 61.38 score is contingent upon the assumed #3 spot in the order; should that shift, his value may recalibrate. Finally, proceed with caution regarding **Kazuma Okamoto** (40.13), as he faces a stiff challenge against Cam Schlittler; his sub-50 score places him on the fringe of our rotation, and he remains the most likely candidate to be pulled for a pinch-hitter if game caps become a concern.",
